# Long-Term Codebase Health Snapshot (Quality Document)

<quality_document version="1.0" framework="RIPER-5">

<!-- Evaluates ongoing codebase health across product domains and architectural layers.
     Update periodically (per sprint, milestone, or significant refactoring) to track
     whether harness improvements and engineering discipline make the system stronger. -->

<metadata>
  <snapshot_id>SNAP-[YYYYMMDD]</snapshot_id>
  <evaluated_date>[YYYY-MM-DD]</evaluated_date>
  <evaluator>[Human Engineer | Non-Implementer Agent]</evaluator>
  <overall_grade>[A | B | C | D]</overall_grade>
</metadata>

---

## 1. Product Domain Quality Grading

<product_domains>
  <!-- Grade scale:
       A: Robust tests, high agent legibility, deterministic verification, zero known gaps.
       B: Solid tests, minor ambiguity in specs or edge cases, reliable in normal runs.
       C: Flaky tests, incomplete verification, agent frequently misinterprets invariants.
       D: Untested, fragile boundaries, high regression rate upon modification. -->

  | Domain / Subsystem | Verification Status | Agent Legibility | Test Stability | Key Gaps | Grade |
  |--------------------|---------------------|------------------|----------------|----------|-------|
  | Core Domain        | Full Automated      | High (Typed AST) | 99% Deterministic | None | A |
  | Auth & Security    | Semi-Automated      | Moderate         | Flaky timeout  | Refresh token race | B |
  | Billing / Payments | Manual E2E only     | Low (Untyped)    | No mocks       | Missing webhook replay | C |
  | Reporting & Export | Automated Unit      | High             | 100%           | Edge case CSV quote | B |
</product_domains>

---

## 2. Architectural Layer Boundary Grading

<architectural_layers>
  | Layer | Boundary Enforcement | Agent Legibility | Coupling Risk | Grade |
  |-------|----------------------|------------------|---------------|-------|
  | Domain Entities & Invariants | Strict Purity (No I/O) | High (Explicit types) | Low | A |
  | Application Use Cases        | Port-based DI          | High                  | Low | A |
  | Infrastructure & Adapters    | Isolated in adapters/  | Moderate              | Medium | B |
  | UI & Presentation            | Component Isolation    | Moderate (DOM tree)   | Low | B |
  | Config & Environment         | Strict validation      | High (.env schema)    | Low | A |
</architectural_layers>

---

## 3. Harness Simplification & Component Ablation Benchmark

<harness_simplification>
  <!-- Every harness component encodes an assumption about what models cannot do.
       As models evolve, run controlled variable exclusion tests:
       1. Record baseline quality snapshot below.
       2. Temporarily remove one harness rule/seed (e.g. detailed prompt constraints).
       3. Run benchmark task suite.
       4. Compare scores: if quality does not degrade, retire the component to reduce token tax. -->

  | Evaluated Component | Removal Date | Benchmark Result | Decision |
  |---------------------|--------------|------------------|----------|
  | [e.g. Detailed syntax prompt] | [YYYY-MM-DD] | Pass rate 100% (No regression) | [RETIRED / RETAINED] |
</harness_simplification>

